---
import InfoPageLayout from '../layouts/InfoPageLayout.astro';
import history from '../data/prc/pnle-history.json';
import prc from '../data/prc/2026.json';
import { formatEditorialDate } from '../lib/editorial';
const held = history.rounds.filter((r) => r.first_date !== null && r.passers !== null && r.examinees !== null);
const minDays = Math.min(...held.map((r) => r.working_days_to_results!));
const maxDays = Math.max(...held.map((r) => r.working_days_to_results!));
---
<InfoPageLayout title="Philippine Exam Data Downloads – PRC and PNLE | AyTool"
  description="Download source-linked PRC 2026 schedules and PNLE results history as CSV or JSON, with field definitions, verification dates and calculation methods."
  path="/data/" h1="Exam Data and Download Library">
  <p>These files are AyTool's independent transcriptions and calculations from linked PRC sources.
    Downloads use the same records as the guides; they are not an official PRC data service.</p>
  <h2>PRC 2026 examination calendar</h2>
  <p>{prc.exams.length} scheduled examination entries, including filing windows, target result dates,
    recorded result releases and source links. Recorded dataset source check:
    <time datetime={prc.meta.last_verified}>{formatEditorialDate(prc.meta.last_verified)}</time>.</p>
  <p><a href="/data/prc-board-exam-schedule-2026.csv" download="aytool-prc-exams-2026.csv">Download PRC schedule CSV</a> ·
    <a href="/data/prc-board-exam-schedule-2026.json">View PRC schedule JSON</a> ·
    <a href="/prc-board-exam-schedule/">Read the calendar and current status</a></p>
  <p><strong>Fields:</strong> examination name, displayed dates, first exam date, filing opening and
    deadline, target release, recorded actual release, passers, examinees, notes and source URLs.
    A target date is not evidence that results were released. Empty result fields mean not recorded here.</p>
  <h2>PNLE results history</h2>
  <p>{history.rounds.length} historical round records, including {held.length} completed sittings with
    counts and the postponed 2020 rounds. Recorded dataset source check:
    <time datetime={history.meta.last_verified}>{formatEditorialDate(history.meta.last_verified)}</time>.</p>
  <p><a href="/data/pnle-results-history.csv" download="aytool-pnle-results-history.csv">Download PNLE history CSV</a> ·
    <a href="/data/pnle-results-history.json">View PNLE history JSON</a> ·
    <a href="/nursing-board-exam-schedule/#pnle-results-history-2019-2026-pass-rates-exam-months-and-re">Read the history table</a></p>
  <h3>How the statistics are calculated</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Pass rate for a sitting = passers ÷ examinees × 100, displayed to two decimal places. Counts come from the linked press release.</li>
    <li>Working days to results are the values recorded for each round. Among completed records here, they range from {minDays} to {maxDays}; postponed rounds with unavailable counts are excluded.</li>
    <li>Counts describe exam sittings, not unique people. Do not sum them and label the result as unique nurses or applicants.</li>
    <li>Null JSON values and blank CSV fields are unavailable or not applicable, not zero. No release date is imputed for a postponed round.</li>
    <li>Each history row keeps its source URL and verification route. Archive-backed records are identified separately.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Using and citing these files</h2>
  <p>Link to the AyTool guide and the original PRC source, identify the year and state when you
    retrieved the file. Check subsequent official notices before relying on a future date.
    For attribution examples and embedding options, see <a href="/for-publishers/">For educators and publishers</a>.</p>
  <p>Found a transcription error? Use the <a href="/corrections/">correction process</a>.</p>
</InfoPageLayout>
